    <string name="consent_title">Before you switch it on</string>
    <string name="consent_body">This app uses Android\'s Accessibility API for one thing: to notice when you open Instagram or YouTube and when you swipe from one video to the next in Reels and Shorts, and to show a small count and Vaathi on top of them.\n\n• It receives two kinds of event, from those two apps only: a window of theirs coming to the front, and something scrolling.\n• It can\'t read what\'s on your screen or what you type, in those apps or any other.\n• It counts your swipes and the time between them, and keeps the counts on this phone.\n• The app has no internet access, so nothing is collected or shared.\n\nOn the next screen, find Vaathi ride-uhh! under installed or downloaded apps and switch it on.</string>
    <string name="consent_agree">I agree</string>
    <string name="consent_decline">Not now</string>

